## 1. Purpose

This report records the execution of the operational qualification and the
acceptance decision for each criterion.

## 2. Acceptance results

Acceptance is decided on a one-sided lower confidence bound. The observed pass
rate describes the sample; the bound is what the sample supports as a claim
about the agent, and is the figure the decision rests on.

A case that failed to execute is excluded from the denominator and reported
separately rather than being counted either way: treating an execution failure
as an agent failure would understate the agent, and dropping it silently would
overstate the evidence base.

